# Third-Party Notices

`maple` is a **clean-room re-implementation** of the reference projects below.
No source code is copied or vendored from them: their source is read as the
specification, and behaviour and file/wire formats are reproduced 1:1 in
freshly written Rust. All code in this repository is written by maple
contributors and licensed under MIT (see `LICENSE`). The clean-room rule
governs the reference source only; maple additionally links third-party
crates.io crates as build dependencies, listed under
[`Runtime dependencies`](#runtime-dependencies) with their licenses.

## References (specification only)

| Project | License | Version read | Used as |
|---|---|---|---|
| [oh-my-pi](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi) | MIT | 18.20.2 (`7c49c11`, 2026-11-14) | TUI renderer model, session/transcript model, hashline edit model, autolearn pipeline, native-module roles |
| [pi-messenger](https://github.com/nicobailon/pi-messenger) | MIT | 0.15.2 | `.pi/messenger` on-disk format and action semantics (registry, inbox, feed.jsonl, reservations, team memory) |

## Compatibility note

maple reads and writes the `.pi/messenger` file format so that existing
pi-messenger agents can interoperate. A file format and an action vocabulary
are not copyrighted expression; no pi-messenger code is included.

